[BIND] The equation is a cubic in $\sin x$, so we can factor it as
\begin{align*}
\sin x(2\sin^2 x - 5\sin x + 2) &= 0,
\end{align*}
which factors further as
\begin{align*}
\sin x(\sin x - 1)(2\sin x - 1) &= 0.
\end{align*}
So the solutions are $\sin x = 0,$ $\sin x = 1,$ or $\sin x = \frac{1}{2}$.
For $0 \le x \le 2\pi$, $\sin x = 0$ has solutions $x = 0$ and $x = \pi$,
$\sin x = 1$ has solution $x = \frac{\pi}{2}$, and $\sin x = \frac{1}{2}$ has solutions $x = \frac{\pi}{6}$ and $x = \frac{5\pi}{6}$.
Thus the total number of solutions is $4.$
